HEADER rung=toy:clean TIMED node <node> arch <arch> v8 <v8> cpu <cpu> K=3 C=3 ops=1024,1024 minWindow=64,64 inject=null
HEADER spec lite-ab-gate-toy lane-file <lane-file> lane-sha256=6810ef7abd25f6e66991020ba8d955e6ffa04846e3b0c8626a939b0bf8549877 transform=k.js:edited | tool <tool>
HEADER frozen k.js frozen/k.js sha256 73e13711 ok; live live/k.js byte-identical -- ok (AB-G2)
HEADER columns: A = base kernel, B = candidate, AA = A twin (fresh compilation), SLOW = A + spin at the A anchor, AB = A twin (fresh compilation) timed at B's reps, present only when B's reps differ from A's (then B/AB and wordAB are printed; else n/a); K + 1 rounds per window, round 0 a warm round discarded from every column (WARM line); flags --expose-gc --allow-natives-syntax --no-concurrent-recompilation --min-semi-space-size=4 --max-semi-space-size=4 --single-threaded-gc
HEADER lane toy:clean A=k.js B=k.js ops=1024 minWindow=64 spin=16 recLen=2
HEADER lane toy:unrolled A=k.js B=k.js ops=1024 minWindow=64 spin=16 recLen=2
HEADER rule: per OS, PASS = every gated lane reads its GATED word with its controls valid (aa median in [0.95, 1.05], slow median > 1.25 and q1 > 1.1, B/AB (B against AB = A at B's reps) reading the same word as B/A when B's reps differ from A's (else REPS-DRIFT; ab = AB / A is REPORTED, no band; equal reps print ab, B/AB, wordAB = n/a), bop A, B, AA, SLOW (+ AB when present) each in [0, 1/64), all finite); FINDING = a clean gated lane reads another word (even with other gated lanes VOID); NO VERDICT = any VOID or missing gated lane, a wrong run shape (one HEADER rung=ALL TIMED with K=11 C=3 and the shape fields, inject=null, one HEADER spec line with this lane file's lane-sha256 and transform=, one PROV start / end, one RESULT per lane) or any STOP / CRASH. NO VERDICT is never a PASS.
HEADER GATED toy:clean=WITHIN; every other lane REPORTED
PROV start <time> load <load> busy-node [<busy>] quiet-lock <quiet-lock>
CONTROL gc-window: empty clean; forced gc flips major (1) -- ok
